{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon","id":1560991,"title":"Can I Play A Toon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-25T13:30:29-07:00","id":1560991,"title":"Can I Play A Toon?","content":"I've asked a different question before about playing a mad scientist but now I have a different question about if I can play a tune this idea comes from Who Framed Roger Rabbit With the Judge I thought it would be interesting to play a character who they have a lot of tune like qualities but leaning into that scary kind of tune where it's just I dropped an anvil on their head I thought they would be fine doesn't hurt me Or making someone laugh to death and they can take abnormal amounts of damage they are just completely out of sync in line with reality even though they look like a normal person Until you run them over with a car and they re inflate themselves. <br /> <br /> I was thinking they would be an outcast or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T15:43:52-07:00","id":1561042,"title":"","content":"Nothing like that currently exists in the canon text, though there are Practices that let you simulate the effects you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T15:22:06-07:00","id":1561063,"title":"","content":"Toon Force is one of the most hideously over powered abilities to exist in all of fiction.<br /> <br /> No, you can not play a Toon, because it would be impossible to balance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T09:33:30-07:00","id":1561079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561063#post1561063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toon Force is one of the most hideously over powered abilities to exist in all of fiction.<br /> <br /> No, you can not play a Toon, because it would be impossible to balance!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true.<br /> <br /> Most of it is fluff, anything can happen to lead to a result, <i>but a Toon is constrained by the result</i>. The central power is only half a dozen effects that are strong, but not that hard to codify:<br /> <br /> - Immortality: nothing can kill a Toon.<br /> <br /> - Regeneration: a Toon won't stay out of action.<br /> <br /> - Toon Access: a Toon's access to an item is a binary state, either too easy or impossible.<br /> <br /> - Physics of Perception: a Toon must follow the same laws as everyone else, but must notice it.<br /> <br /> - Reciprocity: all direct contact follow the Laws of Toon Force \u2013 or not \u2013 without a choice.<br /> <br /> - Presentation: everything a Toon does needs a performance that takes time, effort, and visual.<br /> <br /> What this means as balance:<br /> <br /> 1. Anything that can stop a normal human will in principle stop a Toon. It won't be for long, but it will work.<br /> <br /> 2. The most powerful effect is not staying out of action for long, but not increased power.<br /> <br /> 3. Everything else is two ways. For each effect that benefit a Toon, an equivalent hinder them.<br /> <br /> 4. Surprise effect is strong, but vulnerability to genre understanding too. It's easy to explore Toon Force against a Toon when you're not in turn bound by its laws.<br /> <br /> 5. It's profoundly anti-efficient. A Toon can't do anything the easy way, only the Toon way. That can and will get in the way almost constantly.<br /> <br /> What balances the fabled Toon Force is that it is governed by storytelling. It's unsettling as it won't follow a direct cause -&gt; effect mechanic, but it does follow a meaning -&gt; effect general law that you can interpret through the lens of a Universal Audience, the idea that they're judged by the very audience.<br /> <br /> Other games already worked this, but I'll bring to mind two where those laws have precisely to reconcile with mundane reality: <i><b>Ravenloft</b></i> and <i><b>Changeling the Dreaming</b></i>.<br /> <br /> What both make to ease things out is simply empower the ST/GM with the Storytelling God: the Dark Powers in Ravenloft, the Dreaming in Changeling, are external forces that judge what happens arbitrarily based on genre expectation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T10:06:53-07:00","id":1561080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561079#post1561079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not necessarily true.<br /> <br /> Most of it is fluff, anything can happen to lead to a result, <i>but a Toon is constrained by the result</i>. The central power is only half a dozen effects that are strong, but not that hard to codify:<br /> <br /> - Immortality: nothing can kill a Toon.<br /> <br /> - Regeneration: a Toon won't stay out of action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lots of supernatural creatures can regenerate, that's not the issue. The issue is that a Toon can regenerate back to full health instantly, after being reduced to a pile of ashes.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I had to come up with a rule for keeping them in check, I would abide by the quote of <b><i>&quot;only when it was funny!&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> Which is to say that the Toon Force can only be accessed during a comedically appropriate circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T13:46:22-07:00","id":1561089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561080#post1561080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of supernatural creatures can regenerate, that's not the issue. The issue is that a Toon can regenerate back to full health instantly, after being reduced to a pile of ashes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is impressive only because any damage can visually reduce them to a pile of ashes in the first place.<br /> <br /> And they don't go back to full health instantly, they need a performative action or a cut. This is not passive regeneration.<br /> <br /> Immortality isn't that big of a game change, you can't really solve many problems through the power of not dying failing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T16:58:50-07:00","id":1561178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561079#post1561079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not necessarily true.<br /> <br /> Most of it is fluff, anything can happen to lead to a result, <i>but a Toon is constrained by the result</i>. The central power is only half a dozen effects that are strong, but not that hard to codify:<br /> <br /> - Immortality: nothing can kill a Toon.<br /> <br /> - Regeneration: a Toon won't stay out of action.<br /> <br /> - Toon Access: a Toon's access to an item is a binary state, either too easy or impossible.<br /> <br /> - Physics of Perception: a Toon must follow the same laws as everyone else, but must notice it.<br /> <br /> - Reciprocity: all direct contact follow the Laws of Toon Force \u2013 or not \u2013 without a choice.<br /> <br /> - Presentation: everything a Toon does needs a performance that takes time, effort, and visual.<br /> <br /> What this means as balance:<br /> <br /> 1. Anything that can stop a normal human will in principle stop a Toon. It won't be for long, but it will work.<br /> <br /> 2. The most powerful effect is not staying out of action for long, but not increased power.<br /> <br /> 3. Everything else is two ways. For each effect that benefit a Toon, an equivalent hinder them.<br /> <br /> 4. Surprise effect is strong, but vulnerability to genre understanding too. It's easy to explore Toon Force against a Toon when you're not in turn bound by its laws.<br /> <br /> 5. It's profoundly anti-efficient. A Toon can't do anything the easy way, only the Toon way. That can and will get in the way almost constantly.<br /> <br /> What balances the fabled Toon Force is that it is governed by storytelling. It's unsettling as it won't follow a direct cause -&gt; effect mechanic, but it does follow a meaning -&gt; effect general law that you can interpret through the lens of a Universal Audience, the idea that they're judged by the very audience.<br /> <br /> Other games already worked this, but I'll bring to mind two where those laws have precisely to reconcile with mundane reality: <i><b>Ravenloft</b></i> and <i><b>Changeling the Dreaming</b></i>.<br /> <br /> What both make to ease things out is simply empower the ST/GM with the Storytelling God: the Dark Powers in Ravenloft, the Dreaming in Changeling, are external forces that judge what happens arbitrarily based on genre expectation</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I imagined a toon force as an insanely powerful force but you have to act for the audiance to get more of it and it is a chaotic it wants you to act out and stand out and this can lead to bad things in a dark world of curse born. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T18:00:36-07:00","id":1561180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561178#post1561178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I imagined a toon force as an insanely powerful force but you have to act for the audiance to get more of it and it is a chaotic it wants you to act out and stand out and this can lead to bad things in a dark world of curse born.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about getting more of it and more that it's not something the Toon control.<br /> <br /> A single punch may deform their face. A match is enough to burn down to ashes. They will just be back the next turn or the other, but for at least one action they're out of commission with minimal effort. A beautiful person can likewise demolish resistance, or any emotional response for that matter.<br /> <br /> On most media where Toons and humans interact, Toons have a remarkable hard time actually hurting humans directly, because their actions are always under Toon Physics, this isn't something you can turn off.<br /> <br /> The greatest enemy of a Toon should be the genre-savvy that can understand and use Toon logic against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T02:37:30-07:00","id":1561964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561178#post1561178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah I imagined a toon force as an insanely powerful force but you have to act for the audiance to get more of it and it is a chaotic it wants you to act out and stand out and this can lead to bad things in a dark world of curse born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of, I can think of two examples of how Toon Force applied to the real world would actually be a form of living hell.<br /> <br /> The first example is from D.C comics, in which a character inspired by Wile .E Coyote manages to enter the real world, while retaining all of his cartoon powers. Except that his body isn't a cartoon anymore, it's an anthropomorphic coyote. So every time he gets shot, stabbed, run over, falls off a cliff, exploded, and whatever else typically happens in those old cartoons, it hurts... it hurts a hell of a lot.<br /> <br /> Yes, he manages to regenerate; but his life quickly becomes so miserable, he ends up actively wishing for death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second example is from the Mask comics, in which the main character (known by the alias of the Big Head Killer) dons a magical mask that gives him all the iconic toon force powers. The problem is that these powers only apply to him... not the people around him. This leads to the protagonist inflicting extreme bodily harm upon others, and leaving them in horribly mutilated conditions. Like the time forced a man to swallow an entire car engine, and then left his body chained up in the garage to be discovered by police.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T04:01:43-07:00","id":1561966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561964#post1561964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of, I can think of two examples of how Toon Force applied to the real world would actually be a form of living hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two are deconstructions that don't follow classic toon force, though.<br /> <br /> In the first the point is to not follow Toon Force strictly as a horror/tragedy take on the concept of dimensional travel. The coyote in question is partially stripped of the natural laws of his world for the sake of gore.<br /> <br /> And in The Mask comics the violence is the point. The enchanted mask is a cursed object whose powers are meant to bring chaos and destruction upon the world, making the user increasingly violent, sometimes even without the mask. The appearance of toon force is a style, but the actual magic is something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T13:02:50-07:00","id":1561978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561966#post1561966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The two are deconstructions that don't follow classic toon force, though.<br /> <br /> In the first the point is to not follow Toon Force strictly as a horror/tragedy take on the concept of dimensional travel. The coyote in question is partially stripped of the natural laws of his world for the sake of gore.<br /> <br /> And in The Mask comics the violence is the point. The enchanted mask is a cursed object whose powers are meant to bring chaos and destruction upon the world, making the user increasingly violent, sometimes even without the mask. The appearance of toon force is a style, but the actual magic is something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but this is Curseborne, where every family lineage comes with some sort of drawback in exchange for the powers it offers.<br /> <br /> And in the case of being a Toon, I could see that drawback being one of two options.<br /> <br /> <b>Option A)</b> You become an immortal punching bag, who is regularly tortured for the sake of entertainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Option</b> <b>B)</b> You are so disconnected from reality, that you risk becoming a complete psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T17:28:06-07:00","id":1561981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561978#post1561978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, but this is Curseborne, where every family lineage comes with some sort of drawback in exchange for the powers it offers.<br /> <br /> And in the case of being a Toon, I could see that drawback being one of two options.<br /> <br /> <b>Option A)</b> You become an immortal punching bag, who is regularly tortured for the sake of entertainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Option</b> <b>B)</b> You are so disconnected from reality, that you risk becoming a complete psychopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>The curses are more behavioral, as something the player has autonomy to say when it applies, and the previous question was balance, not curse.<br /> <br /> If Toon Force works like in The Mask, then that is definitely a potential problem, because they (there are several users in the comics, women included) get to follow, ignore or bend the rules for maximum effectiveness.<br /> <br /> Damnations can include several things, but I think it fitting for such a character to have the possibility of becoming a serial killer being put in contrast to an inability to kill directly.<br /> <br /> Since, you know, kill for kill, everyone can do. It is the context for the killing that makes a curse interesting. Look how each Damnation that can lead to this is particular about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T18:51:32-07:00","id":1561983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561981#post1561981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The curses are more behavioral, as something the player has autonomy to say when it applies, and the previous question was balance, not curse.<br /> <br /> If Toon Force works like in The Mask, then that is definitely a potential problem, because they (there are several users in the comics, women included) get to follow, ignore or bend the rules for maximum effectiveness.<br /> <br /> Damnations can include several things, but I think it fitting for such a character to have the possibility of becoming a serial killer being put in contrast to an inability to kill directly.<br /> <br /> Since, you know, kill for kill, everyone can do. It is the context for the killing that makes a curse interesting. Look how each Damnation that can lead to this is particular about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indirect killings does sound like an interesting approach, from a creative standpoint anyways.<br /> <br /> And as any dungeon master knows, your players can, and probably will find a creative away to deal with a seemingly invincible challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-15T18:21:33-07:00","id":1564772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1561063#post1561063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toon Force is one of the most hideously over powered abilities to exist in all of fiction.<br /> <br /> No, you can not play a Toon, because it would be impossible to balance!</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at Road Runner and Wile E Cyote toons are intrinsically over powered but if you wanted to do a comedy game just make everyone toons! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1045-zwyt","name":"Zwyt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-23T05:21:38-07:00","id":1564928,"title":"","content":"You know, those animations about toons breaking the fourth wall and climbing off the page to interact with the real world would serve as a good basis for making them Outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T04:44:50-07:00","id":1564976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1560991-can-i-play-a-toon?p=1564928#post1564928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, those animations about toons breaking the fourth wall and climbing off the page to interact with the real world would serve as a good basis for making them Outsiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've put together a new Lineage (<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/7ey4jcissxso71osq8yt7/Made-the.pdf?rlkey=p727o3bozpmxttoxxvp1mpe1b&amp;st=m0awz4tt&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">the Made</a>) that would be a better fit.<br /> <br /> Here's what Toons might look like as a Family of the Made: <br /> <b><u>THE MADE: FAMILY EXPANSION</u></b><br /> <b><i>THE ANIMATICS (THE CEL-DRAWN)</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You think laughter is innocent? Laughter is kinetic energy, kid. When a safe drops on my head, I see stars and get covered in soot, sure\u2014but keep that turpentine away from me. Turpentine is our silver.&quot;</i><br /> \u2014 <b>Barnaby &quot;Ink-Blot&quot; Finch, Model 1934 Cel-Drawn</b><br /> <br /> <u>OVERVIEW</u> <br /> The Animatics\u2014often called Toons, Ink-Blots, or the Cel-Drawn\u2014are artificial vessels born from high-viscosity India ink, celluloid nitrate sheets, and animator obsession. They catch the Galvanic Spark when a creator\u2019s manic deadlines, hallucinatory exhaustion, or printing press disasters snag on the Web of Curses. Unlike Constructs forged from steel or sculpted from marble, an Animatic is a living illustration given physical mass. They cohabit the physical world as solid, three-dimensional entities, yet their internal chemistry and physical laws remain tied to the drafting table.<br /> <br /> <u>THE LIVED EXPERIENCE &amp; ANATOMY</u> <br /> <b>Pigment and Solvents:</b> An Animatic possesses no blood, bone, or internal organs. Their flesh consists of high-density graphic emulsion over a flexible celluloid skeletal mesh. Inside their skin is thick, staining pigment smelling faintly of vinegar, turpentine, and acetone. When cut or injured, they do not bleed red; their outlines run, streak, and smear like wet India ink.<br /> <br /> <b>The Framerate Uncanny Valley:</b> Under bright, steady light, an Animatic can pass for an eccentric human wearing theatrical makeup. However, when stressed, sprinting, or moving through low light, their spatial motion drops to 12 or 24 frames per second. Mortals observing them experience severe motion sickness: an Animatic's blinks are keyframed, their smiles stretch a fraction of an inch too wide, and their footfalls produce squeaking rubber or clattering woodblock resonance.<br /> <br /> <b>Rubber-Hose Body Horror:</b> The Animatics experience kinetic trauma through elastic deformation. A heavy falling object or blunt impact does not fracture their bones; it flattens their chassis into a disc or stretches their limbs like rubber tubing before popping back into shape. However, this resilience leaves them terrifyingly vulnerable to chemical solvents (&quot;The Dip&quot;), open flame, and intense heat, which dissolve their outlines into un-inked sludge.<br /> <br /> <u>FAMILY MECHANICS</u> <br /> <br /> <b>Path Skills (Pick Three):</b> Artistry/Crafts, Athletics, Performance, Subterfuge. <br /> <b>Major Path Attributes:</b> Dexterity 6, Manipulation 2, Might 2 <br /> <b>Taught Practices:</b> Autonomy, Illusion, Reconfiguration <br /> <br /> <i>MAJOR PATH INHERITANCE: RUBBER-HOSE ELASTICITY</i> <br /> Your chassis deforms and compresses rather than breaking under blunt force.<ul><li>You possess passive <b>Armor 2</b> against blunt kinetic damage, falling impacts, and crushing strikes.</li> <li>Once per scene, you can compress your chassis down to a two-dimensional sheet of paper for up to <b>Composure</b> rounds, allowing you to slide under locked doors, slip through narrow grates, or hide inside flat manila folders.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <i>FAMILY SACRIFICE / SYSTEM STRAIN: PIGMENT BLEBLE</i> <br /> When you overexert your animating current or suffer System Strain, your ink loses structural integrity. Your outline smears, your facial features distort into graphite smudges, and you leave permanent black ink footprints on every surface you touch for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <i>FAMILY MOTIFS</i><ul><li>When casting a spell with the <b>Physical</b> or <b>Trick</b> attunement, bleed 1 Curse Die to extend your melee reach to Medium Range for 1 round as your limbs stretch like rubber tubing.</li> <li>When suffering an injury from blunt kinetic impact, convert 1 level of lethal damage to bashing damage.</li> <li>Spells cast to alter your physical shape or illusionary appearance gain <b>+1 Enhancement</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <u>FAMILY SECRET SPELL: OFF-SCREEN GAG</u><br /> <b>Cost:</b> Bleed 1 Curse Die | <b>Attunements:</b> Magical, Physical, Tech, Trick <br /> <b>Target:</b> Self / Unobserved Space | <b>Range:</b> Touch / Close <br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> You manipulate cinematic framing and spatial blind spots. So long as no mortal or adversary is directly observing an unmonitored space (such as behind your back, inside an empty coat pocket, or around a corner), you can reach into it and pull out a Mundane Item, Stage 1 Relic, or improvised tool that could not plausibly fit there.<br /> <br /> <i>ADVANCES</i> <br /> <b>Pneumatic Pop (Entanglement 2):</b> Hold 1 additional Curse Die. When targeted by a physical attack, you compress entirely into a flattened disc and spring backward across Medium Range, landing unharmed on your feet.<br /> <b>Painted Tunnel (Entanglement 3):</b> Bleed 1 additional Curse Die. You paint a doorway or tunnel onto a solid wall or floor using your own ink. For the duration of the scene, you and your crew can walk through it as if it were an open archway; to anyone else, it remains a flat coat of black paint.<br /> <br /> [h3]STEREOTYPES (IN-FAMILY VOICES)[/h3]<br /> <br /> <b>Prometheans:</b> <i>&quot;Stitched cadavers holding a lightning bolt. They understand what it means to be made from dead parts, but they take themselves way too seriously. Smile a little, Frank.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Chimerics:</b> <i>&quot;Mad-science pets with real fur and teeth. They think they're the ultimate predators until they try biting something that tastes like India ink and turpentine.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Synthetics:</b> <i>&quot;Sleek, silicone, and unblemished. They spend so much energy trying to pass as human that they forget how fun it is to break the rules of geometry.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Forged:</b> <i>&quot;Solid steel and granite. Reliable as an anvil. Just make sure you don't drop one on my head when I'm standing under a spotlight.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sculpted:</b> <i>&quot;Porcelain and marble gallery pieces. They think they own beauty because they were carved in stone. We were drawn frame-by-frame by hand, darling\u2014that's real art.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-26-2026, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T13:11:16-07:00","id":1564981,"title":"","content":"I originally devised the Made to give Frankenstein's Monster a place at the table, as it doesn't fit under any of the official five Lineages. But the Made have turned out to be surprisingly versatile in terms of character concepts they enable, as the Toons illustrate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}